1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,075
Welcome to our lesson on daily life and families. Let's start reading!

2
00:00:06,075 --> 00:00:17,455
Matt works in London, but flats are very expensive there. So, he lives in Barcelona, Spain, where flats are nice and big and not expensive.

3
00:00:17,455 --> 00:00:29,962
He flies from Barcelona to London on Monday, works for three days, and stays with his sister. Then he flies back to Barcelona and works from home two days a week.

4
00:00:29,962 --> 00:00:41,609
Matt doesn’t speak Spanish very well, so he studies at a language school on Saturday. He loves Barcelona; it's a beautiful city and a great place to live.

5
00:00:41,609 --> 00:00:59,252
Which sentence is true about Matt? A: He lives and works in London. B: He lives in Barcelona and works in London. C: He speaks Spanish very well.

6
00:00:59,252 --> 00:01:05,451
The correct answer is B: He lives in Barcelona and works in London.

7
00:01:05,451 --> 00:01:13,508
What does Matt say about flats in London?

8
00:01:13,508 --> 00:01:16,155
They’re very expensive.

9
00:01:16,155 --> 00:01:25,225
Pablo from Spain and Alicia from Argentina are married and live in New York. Their family is truly international!

10
00:01:25,225 --> 00:01:37,905
Alicia's sister Daniela, 46, lives in Buenos Aires with their mother. Her brother Carlos, 37, lives and works in São Paulo, Brazil.

11
00:01:37,905 --> 00:01:47,800
Pablo and Alicia have two children. Their son Alex, 19, is at university in Mexico, where he also lives.

12
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:55,021
Their daughter María, 24, lives in Istanbul with her Turkish husband, Mehmet.

13
00:01:55,021 --> 00:02:04,447
True or False: Pablo and Alicia have two small children.

14
00:02:04,447 --> 00:02:09,303
False. Their children are 19 and 24.

15
00:02:09,303 --> 00:02:17,499
Where does Alicia's brother Carlos live?

16
00:02:17,499 --> 00:02:19,066
Brazil.

17
00:02:19,066 --> 00:02:29,480
Maria writes to Eileen, sharing a photo of her small family on holiday: her husband Greg, daughter Linda, and son Jeff.

18
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:39,418
Her parents, Tom, American, from San Francisco, and Elizabetta, from Warsaw, Poland, are also in the photo.

19
00:02:39,418 --> 00:02:50,102
Maria, a teacher, and Greg, who works in an office, live in Washington with their children. Greg's parents are also in Washington.

20
00:02:50,102 --> 00:02:57,614
However, Maria's parents live in California, so they usually have holidays together.

21
00:02:57,614 --> 00:03:07,575
Maria has two brothers not in the photo: Daniel, an English teacher in Mexico City, and Jon, who lives in Moscow.

22
00:03:07,575 --> 00:03:18,268
Jon's Russian wife, Anna, and their five-year-old daughter, Olga, who speaks Russian and English, sometimes join them for holidays.

23
00:03:18,268 --> 00:03:26,429
Where do Greg and Maria live?

24
00:03:26,429 --> 00:03:28,182
Washington.

25
00:03:28,182 --> 00:03:34,822
Who is Jon's daughter?

26
00:03:34,822 --> 00:03:36,436
Olga.

27
00:03:36,436 --> 00:03:41,605
You've completed the lesson. Keep practicing your English!
